* {{rhymes|en|ʌŋk|s=1}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er}}

# {{cap|intoxicated}} as a result of [[excessive]] [[alcohol]] [[consumption]], [[usually]] by [[drink]]ing [[alcoholic]] [[beverage]]s.
#* {{RQ:R. F. Burton Arabian Nights|night=557|passage=So I took a great dry gourd and, cutting open the head, scooped out the inside and cleaned it; after which I gathered grapes from a vine which grew hard by and squeezed them into the gourd, till it was full of the juice. Then I stopped up the mouth and set in the sun, where I left it for some days, until it became strong wine; and every day I used to drink of it, to comfort and sustain me under my fatigues with that from froward and obstinate fiend; and as often as I drank myself '''drunk''', I forgot my troubles and took new heart.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Dan Shive|title=El Goonish Shive|format=webcomic|date=9 May 2013|section=Comic for Thursday, May 9, 2013|sectionurl=https://www.egscomics.com/comic/2013-05-09|text="What part of 'you got '''drunk'''{{'}} did our parents misunderstand?"  "I only drank a few shots!"}}
# {{lb|en|pejorative}} {{cap|habitually}} or [[frequently]] in a state of [[intoxication]].
# {{lb|en|usually followed by [[with]] or [[on]]}} {{cap|elated}} or [[emboldened]].
#: {{ux|en|'''Drunk''' with power, he immediately ordered a management reshuffle.}}
#* {{RQ:Macaulay History of England|chapter=15|passage='''drunk''' with recent prosperity}}
# {{cap|drenched}} or [[saturated]] with [[moisture]] or [[liquid]].
#* {{RQ:KJV|Deuteronomy|32|42||I will make mine arrows '''drunk''' with blood.}}

